From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: export the boot source in the environment

Boot scripts want to know which medium the BROM loaded the SPL from (to
print it, to pick the root device, to decide whether the SD card is the
boot device at all). Armbian's sunxi boot script reads the boot_media
byte of the SPL header at a hard-coded 0x10028, which is only right for
SoCs whose SRAM A1 is at 0x10000 (A64/H5): on H6/H616/H618 the SPL sits
at 0x20000, on A523 at 0x44000, so there it reports "loaded from SD"
while U-Boot actually came from the SPI flash. U-Boot already knows the
answer (sunxi_get_boot_device(), used for fel_booted/mmc_bootdev), so
publish it as ${boot_source} = fel | mmc0 | mmc2 | spi | nand next to
those two variables. Scripts can then fall back to the SPL header only
on U-Boots that do not export it.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff -ruN a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -835,17 +835,25 @@
 	env_set("fel_booted", NULL);
 	env_set("fel_scriptaddr", NULL);
 	env_set("mmc_bootdev", NULL);
+	env_set("boot_source", NULL);
 
 	boot = sunxi_get_boot_device();
 	/* determine if we are running in FEL mode */
 	if (boot == BOOT_DEVICE_BOARD) {
 		env_set("fel_booted", "1");
+		env_set("boot_source", "fel");
 		parse_spl_header(SPL_ADDR);
 	/* or if we booted from MMC, and which one */
 	} else if (boot == BOOT_DEVICE_MMC1) {
 		env_set("mmc_bootdev", "0");
+		env_set("boot_source", "mmc0");
 	} else if (boot == BOOT_DEVICE_MMC2) {
 		env_set("mmc_bootdev", "1");
+		env_set("boot_source", "mmc2");
+	} else if (boot == BOOT_DEVICE_SPI) {
+		env_set("boot_source", "spi");
+	} else if (boot == BOOT_DEVICE_NAND) {
+		env_set("boot_source", "nand");
 	}
 
 	/* Set fdtfile to match the FIT configuration chosen in SPL. */
